Summary of changes made in this fork (all implemented, see src/component/unified.ts,
src/client/index.ts, and the accompanying tests):
- Removed the bundled React integration (src/react/*) and its
  peer/dev dependencies — this fork is consumed by a SvelteKit
  application, not React.
- Removed the example app, CI workflows, and release-automation
  tooling that shipped with the upstream package.
- Extended the permission-check path (src/component/unified.ts,
  src/component/indexed.ts) and the client (src/client/index.ts) to
  accept a scope *chain* (an array of scopes checked in order, allow-
  anywhere-wins within the chain) instead of a single scope, so an
  organization-wide role assignment can satisfy a restaurant-scoped
  permission check without fanning out one role-assignment row per
  restaurant. Single-scope calls are unaffected.
- Added an `assignableRoles` configuration option, enforced inside
  role-assignment mutations, so that holding a permission to assign
  roles does not implicitly allow assigning a role higher than the
  assigner's own (the upstream package did not guard this).
- Wired up the expired-role/audit-retention cleanup cron
  (src/component/cronSetup.ts's `ensureCleanupCronRegistered`), which
  shipped in upstream but was never actually called from anywhere —
  `assignRole` now registers it idempotently on first use.

